That's totally fine. Thanks!

00:22:10.372 --> 00:22:18.880
Another city light blinks out

00:22:19.089 --> 00:22:28.723
Seems I'm the only one
being left behind like this

00:22:28.932 --> 00:22:37.440
I leaned in close to the light
of the vending machine

00:22:37.649 --> 00:22:46.575
And bought something
other than my usual coffee

00:22:46.783 --> 00:22:51.246
I wonder if I can be myself

00:22:51.454 --> 00:22:57.294
From now on, and even further beyond

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:07.387
Surely someday we'll come
to know sadness as love

00:23:07.596 --> 00:23:16.730
Reconnecting somewhere
and parting again, over and over

00:23:16.938 --> 00:23:30.493
Surely the day will come when we're
all too used to feeling joy

00:23:30.702 --> 00:23:37.042
Call that happiness

00:23:40.045 --> 00:23:41.129
"Next Time"

00:23:41.129 --> 00:23:44.466
"Next Time"
January, a fresh new season.

00:23:44.466 --> 00:23:44.674
"Next Time"

00:23:44.674 --> 00:23:47.552
"Next Time"
But spring is still so far away.

00:23:47.552 --> 00:23:47.761
"Next Time"

00:23:47.761 --> 00:23:51.222
"Next Time" Feelings that were
faintly flickering begin to take shape.

00:23:51.222 --> 00:23:51.431
"Next Time"

00:23:51.431 --> 00:23:55.226
"Next Time" Transparent and undefined like
water scooped and flowing from his hand,

00:23:55.226 --> 00:23:55.435
"Next Time"

00:23:55.435 --> 00:23:58.146
"Next Time"
but still definitely there.

00:23:58.146 --> 00:23:58.355
"Next Time"

00:23:58.355 --> 00:24:02.233
"Next Time"
An important feeling born in his heart.

